  "id": "reel_kubernetes",
  "voice": "en-US-BrianMultilingualNeural",
  "text": "Containers do not exist. There is no tiny virtual machine inside your server. A container is just a normal Linux process, isolated by cgroups and namespaces. When two containers must share memory or localhost, single containers fail. That is why Kubernetes created the Pod. A Pod wraps containers inside the exact same network namespace, letting them talk at lightspeed over localhost. Never deploy bare containers. Deploy Pods.",
